# Normalize line endings so a diff shows the change, not the file.
#
# Without this, the index stores whatever the writer happened to produce. This
# repo has 1535 files stored with LF but checked out as CRLF (i/lf w/crlf) and 19
# stored with CRLF, so the same edit renders as a 370-line rewrite in one file and
# a 4-line change in another depending on which editor touched it. That is how a
# 73-line fix reported as 2415 lines changed - nothing was wrong with the content,
# the diff was simply unreadable.
#
# * text=auto  - git stores LF, checks out native (CRLF here). This is what every
#                other Git project on Windows already relies on, and it is why
#                core.autocrlf is deliberately left alone rather than set here.
# * -text / binary - leave these alone. They are binary or must round-trip byte
#                for byte; normalizing them corrupts them.

* text=auto

# Binary and byte-exact files.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.webp    binary
*.ico     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.zip      binary
*.jar     binary
*.aar     binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks     binary
*.so      binary
*.ttf     binary
*.otf     binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary

# Scripts must stay LF: they run under bash/MSYS and a CRLF shebang fails with
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory".
*.sh      text eol=lf
